  {
    "text": "An illumination source with most pixels in the central obscuration region can increase the process window of contact printing in high-NA EUV lithography, particularly for dynamic random access memory (DRAM) and logic applications.",
    "topic": "memory"
  },
  {
    "text": "The process window enhancement is especially significant for DRAM applications using high-NA EUV lithography.",
    "topic": "memory"
  },
  {
    "text": "The benefit of using central obscuration pixels is less pronounced for configurations with a center-to-center pitch smaller than approximately 30 nm.",
    "topic": "memory"
  },
  {
    "text": "High-NA EUV lithography can be applied to logic and DRAM without needing at-resolution field stitching through innovative design strategies.",
    "topic": "memory"
  },
  {
    "text": "Central obscuration pixels in the illumination source help mitigate the limited depth-of-focus (DOF) challenge in high-NA EUV lithography.",
    "topic": "memory"
  }
]
